<title>USA: Tele-Comms to lay off 250 in California.</title>
<headline>Tele-Comms to lay off 250 in California.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tele-Communications Inc will layoff 250 people who work in areas east of San Francisco, a spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The layoffs are effective April 4.</p>
<p>Many of the workers are part timers who do telemarketing work for TCI, said spokesman Andrew Johnson.</p>
<p>Other workers affected by the layoff are customer service representatives whose work will be shifted to the Denver area, he said.</p>
<p>The layoffs are in addition to ones announced in December in a major cost-cutting plan.</p>
</text>
